    <!-- About screen -->
    <string name="about_title">About</string>
    <string name="about_what_title">What This Is</string>
    <string name="about_what_text">Bible Companion is a free, offline-first Scripture reader and study companion built to help people read the Bible in context. It includes the complete Old and New Testaments in every supported language, plus optional Deuterocanonical, Apocryphal, and Pseudepigraphal collections. Each chapter keeps verse-referenced Bible text together with key takeaways, cross-references, manuscript variants, and translation notes. Scripture remains distinct from editorial study material.</string>
    <string name="about_features_text">Read references inside the app or open them in YouVersion/Bible.com or Bible Gateway. English readers can switch the in-app text between the Berean Standard Bible and the King James Version. Search, text-to-speech, Verse of the Day, reading-position restoration, bookmarks, saved verses, highlights, labels, and visual settings support daily reading. Study tools cover Bible chronology; the genealogy, identity, and divinity of Jesus; the Gospel and grace; canon and translation; Biblical calendars and feasts; Messianic prophecy; Daniel and Revelation timelines; astronomical signs; spiritual warfare; false doctrine; and common distortions of Scripture.</string>
    <string name="about_mission_text">Bible Companion approaches Scripture as truth. It aims for faithful, readable, language-appropriate text; exact references; honest treatment of the divine Name; clear marking of Jesus' words; and candor wherever chronology, manuscript evidence, translation, or historical attribution remains debated. It requires no account, keeps its core content available offline, and exists for serious discipleship and Berean examination of Scripture (Matthew 28:19; Acts 17:11), freely given in the spirit of Matthew 10:8.</string>
    <string name="about_free_text">Free. No ads, subscriptions, accounts, or monetization. All glory to God.</string>
