    <string name="chronology_epoch_psalms">Psalms: Attributions and Traditions</string>
    <string name="chronology_psalms_note">The Psalms span multiple periods; this section groups the collection and does not assign it a single composition date. The non-overlapping groups follow the primary personal attributions in the Hebrew superscriptions. These headings can indicate authorship, dedication, subject, or a musical guild. Jeduthun appears in Psalms 39, 62, and 77 as a musical or performance association. Psalm 88 names both the Sons of Korah and Heman. Bava Batra 14b also preserves a broader tradition that David compiled Psalms through ten elders; it does not assign every psalm individually. Unnamed means the Hebrew superscription names no author.</string>
